\\\  & ={\\int }_{0.4}^{\\infty }8{e}^{-8x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{-8x}{|}_{0.4}^{\\infty } \\\\  & ={e}^{-3.2} \\\\  & ≈0.0408\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-693fb341-39fe-5150-9137-34fee2604c10"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-693fb341-39fe-5150-9137-34fee2604c10" :answer-field/id #uuid "693fb341-39fe-5150-9137-34fee2604c10" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-70d4b207-6b19-5682-92c6-5c0ba818e73a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-70d4b207-6b19-5682-92c6-5c0ba818e73a" "answer-404222de-38b1-5509-b195-dc8a8808dc04" "answer-0720396c-abfc-53ff-8ef1-c514b74b2d21" "answer-c786b93e-93f4-53da-8bd9-45ac133e7e53" "answer-2840ed6b-1f83-568f-87c3-170c58ac5221"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-70d4b207-6b19-5682-92c6-5c0ba818e73a" :answer/id #uuid "70d4b207-6b19-5682-92c6-5c0ba818e73a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.0408" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-404222de-38b1-5509-b195-dc8a8808dc04" :answer/id #uuid "404222de-38b1-5509-b195-dc8a8808dc04" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.0489" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0720396c-abfc-53ff-8ef1-c514b74b2d21" :answer/id #uuid "0720396c-abfc-53ff-8ef1-c514b74b2d21" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.1175" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c786b93e-93f4-53da-8bd9-45ac133e7e53" :answer/id #uuid "c786b93e-93f4-53da-8bd9-45ac133e7e53" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.9512" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2840ed6b-1f83-568f-87c3-170c58ac5221" :answer/id #uuid "2840ed6b-1f83-568f-87c3-170c58ac5221" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.9592" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-9bd8d602-6713-5d8a-8e29-384c77e10125" :question/id #uuid "9bd8d602-6713-5d8a-8e29-384c77e10125" :question/math-academy-id "q-96347" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}(\\frac{1}{3}),$ calculate $P(2<X<3).$ Round your final answer to four decimal places." :question/worked-solution "An exponential random variable $X$ with rate $\\lambda $ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\lambda {e}^{-\\lambda x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that\n\n$$\nX∼\\text{Exp}(\\frac{1}{3}).\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{-x/3}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $P(2<X<3)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(2<X<3) & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{-x/3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{-x/3}{|}_{2}^{3} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-1}+{e}^{-2/3} \\\\  & ≈0.1455\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ebf5a599-01b3-5f07-9129-5e078a5628ad"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ebf5a599-01b3-5f07-9129-5e078a5628ad" :answer-field/id #uuid "ebf5a599-01b3-5f07-9129-5e078a5628ad" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e78e8d34-90e2-5ca7-a750-14ec68adc2ae" :answer-field/choices ["answer-44a2b804-976b-516e-8262-d27bd168e200" "answer-a0f19cf2-ae03-5a5d-a484-a5c96a8a6ed5" "answer-e78e8d34-90e2-5ca7-a750-14ec68adc2ae" "answer-f3ab51fe-7288-559d-9763-4a92ffa3e0fb" "answer-c1c9e78d-99e5-5ab7-9783-9080b7da6c91"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-44a2b804-976b-516e-8262-d27bd168e200" :answer/id #uuid "44a2b804-976b-516e-8262-d27bd168e200" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.1155" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a0f19cf2-ae03-5a5d-a484-a5c96a8a6ed5" :answer/id #uuid "a0f19cf2-ae03-5a5d-a484-a5c96a8a6ed5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.1328" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e78e8d34-90e2-5ca7-a750-14ec68adc2ae" :answer/id #uuid "e78e8d34-90e2-5ca7-a750-14ec68adc2ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.1455" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f3ab51fe-7288-559d-9763-4a92ffa3e0fb" :answer/id #uuid "f3ab51fe-7288-559d-9763-4a92ffa3e0fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.1785" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c1c9e78d-99e5-5ab7-9783-9080b7da6c91" :answer/id #uuid "c1c9e78d-99e5-5ab7-9783-9080b7da6c91" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.1951" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d71bf438-c740-5ac5-956a-edf3ba9d43d6" :question/id #uuid "d71bf438-c740-5ac5-956a-edf3ba9d43d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-96421" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}(1),$ calculate $P(0.5\\le X\\le 2).$ Round your final answer to four decimal places." :question/worked-solution "An exponential random variable $X$ with rate $\\lambda $ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\lambda {e}^{-\\lambda x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that\n\n$$\nX∼\\text{Exp}(1).\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate $P(0.5\\le X\\le 2)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0.5\\le X\\le 2) & ={\\int }_{0.5}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0.5}^{2}{e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{-x}{|}_{0.5}^{2} \\\\  & =-{e}^{-2}+{e}^{-0.5} \\\\  & ≈0.4712\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ab5409cf-4685-540d-8e56-731571e9e2ff"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ab5409cf-4685-540d-8e56-731571e9e2ff" :answer-field/id #uuid "ab5409cf-4685-540d-8e56-731571e9e2ff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ded2a796-947a-596a-9be0-948722eda4df" :answer-field/choices ["answer-13134444-762f-50b4-bf4c-6865257862e6" "answer-ded2a796-947a-596a-9be0-948722eda4df" "answer-8451cd55-2a53-5891-9ae6-f129b4cd4ee2" "answer-486ea7b8-8768-5c1b-9819-16e84f6ed54b" "answer-3b282901-4897-5136-9d46-9253c88fc7f2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-13134444-762f-50b4-bf4c-6865257862e6" :answer/id #uuid "13134444-762f-50b4-bf4c-6865257862e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.4411" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ded2a796-947a-596a-9be0-948722eda4df" :answer/id #uuid "ded2a796-947a-596a-9be0-948722eda4df" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.4712" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8451cd55-2a53-5891-9ae6-f129b4cd4ee2" :answer/id #uuid "8451cd55-2a53-5891-9ae6-f129b4cd4ee2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.4799" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-486ea7b8-8768-5c1b-9819-16e84f6ed54b" :answer/id #uuid "486ea7b8-8768-5c1b-9819-16e84f6ed54b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.4852" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3b282901-4897-5136-9d46-9253c88fc7f2" :answer/id #uuid "3b282901-4897-5136-9d46-9253c88fc7f2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.4885" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-15d3a8f7-57e9-5955-b347-e7b15292f88f" :question/id #uuid "15d3a8f7-57e9-5955-b347-e7b15292f88f" :question/math-academy-id "q-253935" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}(3),$ calculate $P(X\\le \\frac{5}{6}\\,|\\,X>\\frac{2}{3}).$" :question/worked-solution "Given a random variable $X∼Exp(\\lambda ),$ and two positive real numbers $s,t,$ the memoryless property of the exponential distribution states that\n\n$$\nP(X>s+t\\,|\\,X>s)=P(X>t)={e}^{-\\lambda t}.\n$$\n\nWe can compute the complementary conditional probability as follows:\n\n$$\nP(X\\le s+t\\,|\\,X>s)=1-P(X>s+t\\,|\\,X>s)=1-{e}^{-\\lambda t}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $\\lambda =3,$ $s=\\frac{2}{3},$ and $s+t=\\frac{5}{6}.$ From this, we can find $t$ as follows:\n\n$$\nt=(t+s)-s=\\frac{5}{6}-\\frac{2}{3}=\\frac{1}{6}\n$$\n\nSubstituting these values into the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le \\frac{5}{6}\\,|\\,X>\\frac{2}{3}) & =1-{e}^{-\\lambda t} \\\\  & =1-{e}^{-(3)\\cdot (1/6)} \\\\  & =1-{e}^{-1/2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-13285fe0-63a3-5aa6-b3a7-7b2fe9fce9be"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-13285fe0-63a3-5aa6-b3a7-7b2fe9fce9be" :answer-field/id #uuid "13285fe0-63a3-5aa6-b3a7-7b2fe9fce9be" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-bc2d906f-f782-5277-a23b-1b4659529d8e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-bc2d906f-f782-5277-a23b-1b4659529d8e" "answer-016959b9-f05f-53b3-afd3-07e994e53882" "answer-c54104af-76de-56d8-9541-8d02ef24fb4f" "answer-17f972c0-e3f4-509a-b28c-755fd028d943" "answer-8012b58b-be32-5887-bb98-32352b39ab18"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bc2d906f-f782-5277-a23b-1b4659529d8e" :answer/id #uuid "bc2d906f-f782-5277-a23b-1b4659529d8e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-{e}^{-1/2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-016959b9-f05f-53b3-afd3-07e994e53882" :answer/id #uuid "016959b9-f05f-53b3-afd3-07e994e53882" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-{e}^{-1/4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c54104af-76de-56d8-9541-8d02ef24fb4f" :answer/id #uuid "c54104af-76de-56d8-9541-8d02ef24fb4f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-{e}^{-2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-17f972c0-e3f4-509a-b28c-755fd028d943" :answer/id #uuid "17f972c0-e3f4-509a-b28c-755fd028d943" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{-1/2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8012b58b-be32-5887-bb98-32352b39ab18" :answer/id #uuid "8012b58b-be32-5887-bb98-32352b39ab18" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{-4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-a86905dc-6d69-50e5-afb3-4d8bb353dbfd" :question/id #uuid "a86905dc-6d69-50e5-afb3-4d8bb353dbfd" :question/math-academy-id "q-253936" :question/problem "Given that the random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}(\\frac{3}{5}),$ calculate $P(X\\le 9\\,|\\,X>4).$" :question/worked-solution "Given a random variable $X∼Exp(\\lambda ),$ and two positive real numbers $s,t,$ the memoryless property of the exponential distribution states that\n\n$$\nP(X>s+t\\,|\\,X>s)=P(X>t)={e}^{-\\lambda t}.\n$$\n\nWe can compute the complementary conditional probability as follows:\n\n$$\nP(X\\le s+t\\,|\\,X>s)=1-P(X>s+t\\,|\\,X>s)=1-{e}^{-\\lambda t}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $\\lambda =\\frac{3}{5},$ $s=4,$ and $s+t=9.$ From this, we can find $t$ as follows:\n\n$$\nt=(t+s)-s=9-4=5\n$$\n\nSubstituting these values into the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 9\\,|\\,X>4) & =1-{e}^{-\\lambda t} \\\\  & =1-{e}^{-(3/5)\\cdot (5)} \\\\  & =1-{e}^{-3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3a0a548f-8bd4-50d5-8207-5dc86f15188f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3a0a548f-8bd4-50d5-8207-5dc86f15188f" :answer-field/id #uuid "3a0a548f-8bd4-50d5-8207-5dc86f15188f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5151c7de-e2f6-5856-b422-07c5dab2d5f4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-25fb97a5-9ed6-5c98-8031-485552414117" "answer-f5b3ce16-7f1a-5313-be26-0788d6b661a0" "answer-5151c7de-e2f6-5856-b422-07c5dab2d5f4" "answer-e5bcecd5-8331-5e54-9822-a05d7243d9b8" "answer-4cbd30f8-0317-54c7-8a80-7f23503ecca6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-25fb97a5-9ed6-5c98-8031-485552414117" :answer/id #uuid "25fb97a5-9ed6-5c98-8031-485552414117" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-5{e}^{-3/5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validat